  "story": "Hoot was a wise owl who cared for an ancient library. One evening, Mina arrived seeking secret knowledge to help her grandmother sleep. Hoot offered tea, opened his notebook, and promised they would search together.\n\nThe index pointed to a moonlit recipe, but its stand was empty. Mina worried they had come too late. Hoot studied the dusty floor and found a trail of silver letters leading toward the tallest shelf.\n\nMina climbed the rolling ladder while Hoot held it steady. They followed the letters to a book wrapped in blue cloth. Inside, a recipe described a soothing drink, yet one important line was hidden beneath a fold.\n\nA torn corner concealed the final instruction. Mina sighed, and Hoot nearly guessed the missing words. Instead, he closed the book. A good helper checks carefully, he explained, especially when someone dear is waiting at home.\n\nMoonlight slipped through the window and revealed faint writing on the reverse. Together they read the missing instruction: stir slowly while remembering a happy moment. Mina copied it carefully, and Hoot packed the book for her.\n\nMina hurried home with the recipe and returned the next morning smiling. Her grandmother had slept peacefully. She gave Hoot a copy for the library, where secret knowledge became a gift that everyone could share.",
