  "schema_version": 2,
  "story": "Nova was a space explorer visiting a blue alien planet. She collected pictures, not rocks, so discoveries could stay beautiful for everyone. Her orange patches stood out against the curling silver plants near the rocket.\n\nThree friendly aliens waved beside a silent windmill. Their leader offered Nova a map covered in musical notes. A puzzling beep came from the machine, and Nova realized the visitors were asking for help, not hiding treasure.\n\nNova turned the map upside down and matched its notes to the windmill wheels. She tightened the loosest wheel while the aliens watched. A soft hum began, but the sails still refused to turn in the breeze.\n\nDust swirled around her boots, and a silver vine caught in the sail. Nova pulled too quickly, making the knot tighter. She sat down and took a breath. Exploring a new world meant learning its rules first.\n\nNova noticed the vine bent toward music. She hummed the map’s gentlest note, and the aliens joined in. The vine relaxed, the sail slipped free, and the windmill spun, sending warm light across their blue world.\n\nThe friendly aliens invited Nova to picnic beneath the glowing sails. She added their song to her discoveries. As her rocket lifted toward the stars, Nova waved, knowing every new world held friends to understand.",
